 <212658678+luuoaoa@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 15 Aug 2026 10:26:59 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Recommend Telex, not TCVN, as the Vietnamese input method
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A Vietnamese profile came up on TCVN, an encoding-era layout almost nobody
types with. Everything about it looks right -- the tray says VI, the IME is
active, keys arrive -- but Telex sequences pass through as plain letters, so
"tieengs" stays "tieengs". There is nothing on screen to explain it, and the
four Vietnamese methods are hard to tell apart, so the machine simply looks
like it cannot type Vietnamese.

The choice comes from one line of kDefaultInputMethodRecommendation in
input_method_util.cc, consulted before the component extension manager has
finished loading. Not the region's keyboard list, and not the order of
m17n_manifest.json -- both of which I changed first, and neither of which had
any effect.

Verified: a fresh local account now preloads vkd_vi_telex, and typing
"tieengs Vieejt ddaay nguwowfi" on a hardware keyboard gives
"tiếng Việt đây người".

---
 ui/base/ime/ash/input_method_util.cc | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/ui/base/ime/ash/input_method_util.cc b/ui/base/ime/ash/input_method_util.cc
index 771e14315c..b1b27fc0b0 100644
--- a/ui/base/ime/ash/input_method_util.cc
+++ b/ui/base/ime/ash/input_method_util.cc
@@ -72,7 +72,11 @@ const struct {
     {"zh-CN", "", "zh-t-i0-pinyin"},
     {"zh-TW", "", "zh-hant-t-i0-und"},
     {"th", "", "vkd_th"},
-    {"vi", "", "vkd_vi_tcvn"},
+    // NOTE(colorburst fork): upstream recommends TCVN. Telex is what
+    // Vietnamese typists overwhelmingly use; TCVN is a legacy encoding-era
+    // layout. Landing a Vietnamese profile on TCVN means Telex sequences
+    // arrive as plain letters, which reads as "typing is broken".
+    {"vi", "", "vkd_vi_telex"},
     {"ru", "", "xkb:ru::rus"},
 };
 
